==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From the {{der|is|non|skyr||thick curdled milk|lit=separated}}, from {{m|non|skera|t=to divide}}. <ref>J.Fritzner. Ordbog over det gamle norske Sprog. 1862, Christiania.</ref><ref>{{R:ine:IEW|938-947}}</ref><ref>{{R:American_Heritage_Dictionary|scurvy}}</ref>

Related to the terms {{cog|da|skør|pos=dialect}}, {{m|da|skørost|pos=dialect}}, {{cog|nn|skyr||buttermilk, cultured milk}}, {{m|nn|skjør}}, {{m|nn|skjørost}}, and many similar terms in Swedish dialects. The Latin term {{m|la|[[lac]] [[concresco|concretum]]||thick milk}} is found in {{w|Tacitus|Tacitus'}} ''{{w|Germania (book)|Germania}}''. Possibly borrowed into English as {{cog|en|scurvy}}.

